WEBVTT

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:06.650
The Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament Semifinals.

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:11.990
The fierce fight concluded with
Satoshi defeating the Champion of Sinnoh, Shirona,

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:13.990
advancing to the finals at last.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:21.580
With tomorrow’s decisive match ahead of them,
Satoshi and Go have arrived at Shoot Stadium.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:25.460
I wonder what Mr. Dande
wants to show us.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:27.840
Maybe the Pokémon
he’s gonna use in the finals?

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:33.810
Mr. Dande!

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:34.890
Hey.

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:37.230
Ms. Sonia!
Professor Magnolia!

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:38.560
Hello!

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.270
Nice to see you two again!

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:43.360
I’ve been watching your battles, Satoshi.
You’re amazing!

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:46.070
You’ve made it this far,
so give Dande a good thrashing, too!

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:47.030
Yeah!

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:49.570
Hey, Sonia...
Don’t be like that.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:51.240
Um...

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:53.660
What was it
you wanted to show us?

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:54.950
This.

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:55.990
Come on out!

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:02.830
Mugendaina!

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:45.900
Surprised?

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:47.810
Uh... Um... Yeah...

00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:52.030
That thing was so violent...

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:55.450
Which is why I left it
with Professor Magnolia...

00:02:55.990 --> 00:03:01.620
After that, we temporarily stored Mugendaina
deep beneath the laboratory.

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:05.540
But if we just leave it to slumber,
there’ll be no future for us.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:09.670
Mugendaina is deeply connected
with Galar particles,

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:12.760
the energy that flows
throughout our region of Galar.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:16.760
It’s an integral part
of the lives of the people of Galar.

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:22.060
We need to coexist
with Mugendaina.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:26.890
And that’s why we thought we’d start
by getting it used to human contact.

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:29.060
With a bit of help from Dande.

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:32.570
It was a tough job at first,
since it kept lashing out at me,

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:34.610
but look at it now!

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.820
Whoa... Awesome!

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:43.120
Now, if it can just learn to
control its power a bit more...

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:46.080
Um... Mr. Dande!

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:50.500
Can I...
leave Mugendaina with you?

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:51.290
<i>Huh?</i>

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:52.090
Go...

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:55.880
It’s an important Pokémon
to the people of Galar...

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:57.590
And...

00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:02.310
I feel like Mugendaina’s
accepted you too, Mr. Dande.

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:03.430
Go...

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:04.850
Are you really sure?

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:05.890
Yes!

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:11.860
Someday, I want to become an amazing trainer
that Mugendaina will accept, like you!

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:16.110
Got it.
I’ll honor your wish.

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:25.580
Mr. Dande, make sure
you don’t get lost tomorrow!

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:27.660
You’re a cheeky one, Satoshi,
you know that?

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:29.370
I have Lizardon, so I’ll be fine!

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:33.040
Good luck, Lizardon...

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:37.380
So, what are your plans for today?

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:39.760
Training to prepare for tomorrow?

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:41.430
Nope, I won’t do anything.

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:42.090
Huh?

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:44.720
We’ve made it this far.
No point sweating it now!

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:48.230
We’ll have a good rest tonight
so we can fight at full power!

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:49.600
Right, Pikachu?

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:52.770
So we should start with
some good food.

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:57.280
The really nice-smelling
tiny thingies!

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:58.650
They’re scones.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:01.320
I choose them...

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:02.820
Right, right...

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:04.700
Aceburn?!

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:11.120
Do you remember this place,
Aceburn?

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:16.800
This is where we met.

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:20.720
Mister!

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:22.800
Hello!

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:24.640
Oh, it’s you kids.

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:25.680
Have you been well?

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:26.470
Yeah!

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:27.560
Look at this!

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:31.310
The Hibunny from back then
has evolved into Aceburn!

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:34.230
Huh?
This is that same Hibunny?!

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:39.070
Come on, stop it!

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:40.780
What’s going on?!

00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:42.200
What are those...?

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:50.330
Zigzaguma: Galarian Form!
Tiny Raccoon Pokémon! Evil/Normal type!

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:53.170
It runs in zigzags and wreaks havoc
upon its surroundings!

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:57.380
Somebody!

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:04.760
Look, Aceburn!

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:08.720
It’s your old followers,
the mischievous Kusune!

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:21.990
Thank you!

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:23.490
Hold on just a sec.

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:25.990
Here, have this as thanks.

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:29.080
Thanks for always helping!

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:31.660
Thank you for protecting our city!

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:32.960
Have this!

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:35.710
We’re counting on you!

00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:36.460
Thanks.

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:40.340
Thank you.

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:42.720
Here’s hoping you keep it up!

00:06:57.190 --> 00:06:58.560
As you can see...

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:03.280
They stopped stealing, and started helping people
and punishing mischievous Pokémon...

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:06.110
Now they’re famous around here.

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:07.700
Ooh!

00:07:36.190 --> 00:07:41.190
Tomorrow, we’re taking that strongest guy’s Pokémon
and the brat boy’s Pokémon all in one go!

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:43.150
Is that really going to work,
though...?

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:47.110
We just need to prepare
lots of strong Pokémon ourselves, meow.

00:07:49.450 --> 00:07:51.200
Forget that, I’m hungry...

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:19.190
Don’t they look pretty evil?

00:08:19.190 --> 00:08:21.480
Don’t they look a lot like Nyarth?

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:22.520
They even have Charms...

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:27.780
What, meow?!
They’re not clean and tidy like me at all, meow!

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:30.240
Nyarth: Galarian Form.

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:31.030
What?!

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:31.950
See, I told you.

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:33.490
Don’t interrupt me!

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:36.660
And the bigger one
is the evolved form, Nyaiking.

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:41.210
With them on our side, we could
get our hands on plenty of food or Pokémon.

00:08:41.210 --> 00:08:43.670
We should try and
recruit them somehow.

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:48.550
That decided, I’ll make them my underlings
and form a Nyarth Army, meow.

00:08:50.260 --> 00:08:51.840
Hey, you guys.

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:55.260
Ready? Listen up!

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:57.810
You’re going to be
my underlings, meow.

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:07.940
They’re all good!

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:11.700
You too, Pikachu and Sarunori!

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:16.330
What’s wrong, Go?

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:17.160
Nothing...

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:21.210
I was just thinking about
how much began right here...

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:25.340
I had decided Mew was going to be
the first Pokémon I caught...

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:27.800
...but when I met Hibunny,

00:09:28.510 --> 00:09:30.930
and it wound up being
my first catch instead,

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:33.220
that’s when my new dream was born.

00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:38.100
To catch every Pokémon
and work my way up to Mew...

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:40.230
Yeah, that’s right.

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:43.020
And now,
I might finally get to meet Mew.

00:09:50.320 --> 00:09:52.150
Did something happen?

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:54.990
Give that back!

00:09:56.580 --> 00:09:57.910
Give me that!

00:09:57.910 --> 00:09:59.660
What’re you doing?!

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:01.160
Hey!

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:02.330
Stop!

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:03.500
Who are they?

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:05.170
Nyaiking and the Nyarth.

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:09.550
They turned up recently,
and have been running wild.

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:35.610
After them, Go!

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:36.410
Right!

00:10:45.170 --> 00:10:48.130
Which way did they go?

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:00.430
A catch already!

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:02.600
Keep this up,
and whether it’s Pokémon or food...

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:05.230
...we’ll be raking ‘em in, meow!

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:13.320
Pocket Monsters!

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:26.080
Hey! Kusune!

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:28.670
Where could they have gone?

00:11:30.340 --> 00:11:34.090
This fountain...
I caught Messon here.

00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:36.880
Of course!

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:38.470
Inteleon!

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:43.600
Inteleon,
we’re chasing after some Kusune.

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:45.810
Can you help us look for them?

00:12:06.660 --> 00:12:08.580
Satoshi, this way!

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:09.670
Got it!

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:20.180
Give it up!
You’re not getting away!

00:12:20.180 --> 00:12:22.550
You’re going to
serve Team Rocket!

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:26.140
All thanks to our
Boss Nyaiking!

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:28.770
Marvelous job luring them here!

00:12:28.770 --> 00:12:33.360
Please keep it up!
Keep bringing us food and Pokémon, meow!

00:12:37.570 --> 00:12:41.070
So... how did <i>we</i> end up
the underlings?

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:44.950
Relax...
Flattery is the road to success.

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:52.080
Team Rocket!

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:54.920
So you were the ones
controlling Nyaiking!

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:56.210
Nonsense!

00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:59.300
We are underlings
of the great Nyaiking!

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:02.220
<i>It’s</i> the one that’s
controlling <i>us,</i> meow!

00:13:03.350 --> 00:13:04.720
What?

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:05.970
Well, whichever way it is,

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:08.230
you’re gonna give back
everyone’s food!

00:13:08.230 --> 00:13:09.980
Humph!
The brat’s mouthing off.

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:12.940
We’ll help ourselves to Pikachu,
and your Pokémon, too!

00:13:12.940 --> 00:13:14.020
Hold on, Musashi!

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:14.570
Huh?

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:17.990
The plan is to take
the brat boy’s Pokémon tomorrow.

00:13:17.990 --> 00:13:18.990
Oh, right.

00:13:18.990 --> 00:13:20.490
Then...

00:13:20.490 --> 00:13:21.360
Do we just back off?

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:23.370
What are you saying, meow?

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:27.080
Don’t put off until tomorrow
any evil you can do today, meow!

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:29.080
Oh, Nyarth...!

00:13:29.080 --> 00:13:30.750
You’re the gold standard of evil!

00:13:30.750 --> 00:13:33.250
Vending, come on, meow!

00:13:42.260 --> 00:13:43.010
Rocket!

00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:44.470
Vending!

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:46.890
Secret!

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:49.270
What’re we gonna get?!

00:13:51.020 --> 00:13:54.060
The Serene Pokémon,
Tebrim!

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:56.320
The Devious Pokémon,
Gimoh!

00:13:57.110 --> 00:13:59.110
Better get ready, brat boy!

00:13:59.530 --> 00:14:00.860
Let’s move, Pikachu!

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:04.490
Aceburn?

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:11.870
Of course... Got it!

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:15.130
Satoshi, can you let us
handle this on our own?

00:14:15.460 --> 00:14:16.750
Go...

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:18.000
All yours!

00:14:18.630 --> 00:14:21.510
Thanks! All right...

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:25.300
Let’s move!
Aceburn! Inteleon! Sarunori!

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:30.680
Didn’t think we were done,
did ya?

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:33.020
Every Charm gives us
a spin of the Vending!

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:34.270
What?!

00:14:34.650 --> 00:14:35.270
Rocket!

00:14:35.650 --> 00:14:36.650
Vending!

00:14:36.650 --> 00:14:38.440
Secret!

00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:40.900
Rocket!

00:14:41.320 --> 00:14:42.320
Vending!

00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:44.110
Secret!

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:47.030
It’s a Vending fever!

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:52.620
The Big Rock Pokémon,
Ishihengin!

00:14:53.290 --> 00:14:55.920
The Sheep Pokémon,
Baiwooloo!

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:59.800
The Rush Pokémon,
Sashikamasu!

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:03.380
The Gulp Pokémon,
U'u!

00:15:07.640 --> 00:15:09.390
You still got this, Go?

00:15:09.390 --> 00:15:10.260
Yeah!

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:13.930
If I couldn’t handle this,
I’d never be able to reach Mew, yeah?

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:19.610
We have Boss Nyaiking
on our side, too!

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:37.370
Tebrim! Brutal Swing!
Ishihengin! Stomp!

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:39.040
Baiwooloo! Tackle!

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:46.090
Dodge, Aceburn, Inteleon!

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:49.640
Gimoh! Surprise Attack!

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:21.840
What is that?!

00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:24.050
A Sashikamasu projectile
from the mouth?!

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:34.430
I have to stop it!

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:36.270
Sarunori, go for it!

00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:54.660
The Kusune!

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:56.160
They evolved!

00:16:58.290 --> 00:17:01.330
Foxly! Fox Pokémon!
Evil type!

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:06.000
It steals its pickings with its lithe body
and sharp claws!

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:42.170
Boss Nyaiking!

00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:10.190
Now, Aceburn! Pyro Ball!

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:24.540
Inteleon, use Snipe Shot!

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:43.810
You’ve gotta be kidding me!

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:45.600
They were all defeated!

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:48.230
Kojiro! The Vending!
Vending!

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:49.730
Rocket...

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:51.490
Huh?

00:18:51.490 --> 00:18:53.650
What <i>now?</i>

00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:55.780
This guy doesn’t fit
in the Vending!

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:57.370
How come, meow?

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:09.170
Aceburn! Pyro Ball!

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:25.310
<i>For the first time in ages,
what an awful feeling!</i>

00:19:31.530 --> 00:19:33.280
You showed ‘em!

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:47.290
Here!
To celebrate you evolving!

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:50.040
Continue keeping our city safe, okay?

00:19:52.050 --> 00:19:54.050
Good for you!

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:18.700
Now, you must be
hungry too, no?

00:20:18.700 --> 00:20:20.700
Thank you!

00:20:32.090 --> 00:20:33.210
The Foxly...

00:20:34.090 --> 00:20:38.010
They’re taking after
your spirit as a street gang boss!

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:50.440
We ate all we could,

00:20:50.440 --> 00:20:53.190
now just gotta sleep for tomorrow!

00:20:53.820 --> 00:20:56.110
You really are battling Mr. Dande...

00:20:56.110 --> 00:20:58.570
I’m so excited,
I might not get any sleep.

00:21:04.790 --> 00:21:06.240
What’s wrong, Go?

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:09.210
I’m sorry, Satoshi...

00:21:09.210 --> 00:21:09.710
I...

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:12.540
...can’t watch your
battle tomorrow.

00:21:13.960 --> 00:21:17.300
I got an urgent summons
from Project Mew.

00:21:17.300 --> 00:21:19.380
So I have to leave right now...

00:21:20.590 --> 00:21:24.050
Really?
Well, make sure you meet that Mew!

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:27.310
Yeah! Make sure you
win too, Satoshi!

00:21:27.310 --> 00:21:28.480
Yeah!

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:30.850
It’s a promise!

00:21:30.850 --> 00:21:32.480
Next time we meet...

00:21:32.480 --> 00:21:34.400
...let’s meet with a smile!

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:37.320
To achieve their own dreams,

00:21:37.320 --> 00:21:40.360
Satoshi and Go each depart
on separate paths.

00:21:40.990 --> 00:21:42.660
And waiting
before them...

00:23:06.160 --> 00:23:08.530
The Pokémon World Championships!

00:23:06.170 --> 00:23:08.520
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:23:08.520 --> 00:23:15.560
I’ve got my plans for when I grow up in my pocket

00:23:08.530 --> 00:23:11.490
Will we see the single biggest upset in history?!

00:23:12.040 --> 00:23:16.290
The exhilarating Masters Tournament
is finally about to reach its climax!

00:23:16.290 --> 00:23:19.670
The absolute monarch, Competitor Dande,
has won his way through the ranks!

00:23:16.500 --> 00:23:21.680
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:23:19.670 --> 00:23:24.510
Facing him is a first-time
Masters Tournament entrant and first-time finalist,

00:23:21.680 --> 00:23:26.000
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:23:24.510 --> 00:23:26.970
the promising rising star,
Competitor Satoshi!

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:26.970
Let’s have a fight!

00:23:26.970 --> 00:23:29.510
Which one will be the world’s strongest?!

00:23:27.290 --> 00:23:29.510
1. Once the battle’s done

00:23:29.510 --> 00:23:33.520
On the next episode,
complete coverage of the exhilarating finals!

00:23:29.890 --> 00:23:31.910
2. And we’re laughing or crying

00:23:31.910 --> 00:23:35.440
On 3, let’s be...

00:23:33.520 --> 00:23:35.440
Don’t miss it!
